  "interpretations": [
    {
      "id": "C1-consent-system-level",
      "text": "For placing on the market or putting into service, the consent element of point (ba) is read at system level: the point is not met where the system generates or manipulates the material only with the depicted person's consent. Art. 5(1a)(a) frames its conditions at system level ('design, training, architecture, capabilities'), and Recital 12 asks for means to collect and demonstrate consent."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2-use-limb",
      "text": "Art. 5(1a)(b) is read literally: the use is prohibited only where the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance; the content element stays and the Art. 5(1a)(a) conditions do not apply to use."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3-roles",
      "text": "Providers (Art. 3(3)) and importers (Art. 3(6)) place on the market or put into service and are tested under Art. 5(1a)(a); deployers (Art. 3(4)) use and are tested under Art. 5(1a)(b). A distributor makes available (Art. 3(7)), which is not the first making available that Art. 3(9) calls placing on the market, so a distributor-only profile stays UNKNOWN and goes to review."
    }
  ],
